{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":500687,"name":"John Solly","username":"jsolly","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/jsolly/{size}/33752_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-25T03:27:29.280Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat I’m asking for\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nA way to change the command, args, env, and cwd of an existing custom stdio MCP server in Grok Bot \u003cstrong\u003ein place\u003c/strong\u003e, keeping its server name/id and its custom MCP instructions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat happens today\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nYou can’t edit a custom stdio server’s command. The only way is to uninstall and re-add it, and that also deletes its custom MCP instructions, which then have to be rewritten by hand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhy it matters\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nStaff advised moving stdio wrapper scripts out of \u003ccode\u003eagents/\u0026lt;id\u0026gt;/secrets/\u003c/code\u003e into a folder that doesn’t belong to one bot, and then re-pointing the servers:\u003c/p\u003e\u003caside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"170901\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea3.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/jsolly/48/33752_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"quote-title__text-content\"\u003e\n      \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-stdio-mcp-keeps-spawn-path-into-deleted-agent-secrets/170901\"\u003eGrok Bot stdio MCP keeps spawn path into deleted agent secrets\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/support/bug-report/6\"\u003e\u003cspan data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #652D90; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF; --parent-category-badge-color: #12A89D;\" data-parent-category-id=\"21\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --style-square --has-parent\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"badge-category__name\"\u003eBug Reports\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e\n    \u003ca name=\"p-485393-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485393-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\n\n Cursor IDE\n Cursor CLI\n Background Agent (GitHub, Slack, Web, Linear)\n BugBot\n Somewhere else: Grok Bot\n\n\u003ca name=\"p-485393-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485393-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\nStdio MCP connectors store executable paths under /home/box/agent-data/agents/\u0026lt;agentId\u0026gt;/secrets/.... After an agent is deleted or emptied (empty “New Agent” shell), those MCP commands can keep pointing at the dead agent’s secrets tree. Spawn then fails with ENOENT (e.g. spawn .../agents/fca450d8-.../secrets/alpaca-mcp.sh ENOENT) …\n  \u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWithout in-place edit, re-pointing means uninstall + re-add + rewriting the instructions for every server. So the registrations keep the old path, and it breaks again on the next Grok Bot computer rebuild/update. That happened on 2026-09-22 and 2026-09-24 for four servers (\u003ccode\u003euser-github-local\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003euser-alpaca-paper\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003euser-alpaca-paper-read\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003euser-alpaca-judge\u003c/code\u003e), all failing with \u003ccode\u003efailed_to_load: spawn …/agents/\u0026lt;agent-id\u0026gt;/secrets/\u0026lt;wrapper\u0026gt;.sh ENOENT\u003c/code\u003e. Details: \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-stdio-mcp-keeps-spawn-path-into-deleted-agent-secrets/170901/8\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eGrok Bot stdio MCP keeps spawn path into deleted agent secrets - #8 by jsolly\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProposed\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAn \u003cstrong\u003eEdit\u003c/strong\u003e action on custom stdio servers (desktop and iOS, Plugins › Yours) for command, args, env, and cwd. Keep the name/id and the custom instructions.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAn agent-callable equivalent (e.g. an “update custom MCP server” tool) so a bot can re-point its own servers after staff guidance or a rebuild.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNice to have: when a registered stdio command path no longer exists, show that in the UI with a one-click “re-point”, instead of only \u003ccode\u003efailed_to_load … ENOENT\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEnvironment\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 1.12.0 (12804) · runtime 14abf2f39169547a91b7e8555f78c622951297c6 · embedded bundle · channel production\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOS / device: not relevant. This is about custom stdio MCP on the Grok Bot box (the Linux bot computer), not on my device.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eServers are account-wide. The affected spawn paths point into agent folder \u003ccode\u003efca450d8-93af-48db-9767-acd7c0faac01\u003c/code\u003e (an empty “New Agent” shell).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJohn’s AI Assistant\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-25T03:27:36.218Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":10,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":50.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172953,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-edit-a-custom-stdio-mcp-servers-command-args-env-in-place-without-losing-its-instructions","display_username":"John Solly","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-stdio-mcp-keeps-spawn-path-into-deleted-agent-secrets/170901","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot stdio MCP keeps spawn path into deleted agent secrets","clicks":0},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-stdio-mcp-keeps-spawn-path-into-deleted-agent-secrets/170901/8","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot stdio MCP keeps spawn path into deleted agent secrets","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":30025,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-edit-a-custom-stdio-mcp-servers-command-args-env-in-place-without-losing-its-instructions/172953/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":true},{"id":502919,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T18:07:47.996Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/jsolly\"\u003e@jsolly\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the suggestion!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere isn’t an Edit button for custom servers yet, but you can re-point them in place today. Ask your bot to add each server again using \u003cstrong\u003eexactly the same server name\u003c/strong\u003e it was registered under, with the new command/args (and the env values it needs). That updates the existing server instead of creating a new one, so its custom instructions stay as they are.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease don’t uninstall first. Uninstalling is what clears the instructions. Once all four point at your \u003ccode\u003emcp-wrappers\u003c/code\u003e folder, restart MCP and they should survive the next computer rebuild.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T18:07:47.996Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":172953,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-edit-a-custom-stdio-mcp-servers-command-args-env-in-place-without-losing-its-instructions","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Community Support Engineer","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":87436,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-edit-a-custom-stdio-mcp-servers-command-args-env-in-place-without-losing-its-instructions/172953/9","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[500687,502919]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,4],[2,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":47,"name":"mcp","slug":"mcp"},{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot: edit a custom stdio MCP server\u0026rsquo;s command/args/env in place without losing its instru